    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45914" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subjectīvus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		subjectus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the
			subject</i> of a proposition, <i>subjective</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pars,</span>”
				i. e. <i>the subject</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">App. Dogm. Plat. 3, p. 30, 30</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 4, § 393</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Tert. Virg. Vel. 4</span></i>
			<i>fin.—Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subjectīvē</span></b> , <i>subjectively</i>, <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 4,
				§ 393</span></i>.</div>
